{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/codex_memory.md'\"","aggregated_output":"# AdaRES_project Research Memory\n\n## Goal And Phase\n- Phase 1 ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515 unmet; Phase 2 pending. server-2 GPUs 0/1 only, one single-GPU experiment per card; server-6 excluded.\n- Released SPFormer sparse-UNet backbone and project decoder. No validation tuning of thresholds, temperatures, weights, features, margins, occupancy weight or the fixed 30-epoch protocol.\n\n## Champion And Baseline\n- B1 0.5020 mIoU, Acc@0.25 0.610, Acc@0.5 0.553, spmIoU 0.467.\n- B4-E30 champion 0.5094, Acc@0.25 0.608, Acc@0.5 0.562, spmIoU 0.474 at epoch 27; target gap 0.0056. It preserved epoch-20 optimizer/scheduler state, not a separate fresh seed-matched run.\n- B4-E30 best.pth: /bak_home/songcl/Project/AdaRES_project/AdaRES_checkpoints/adares_b4_query_competition_res/20260921_210214/best.pth.\n\n## Active Hypotheses\n- G1 replaces seed/object indicator labels with detached per-query predicted-mask IoU against training target. Fixed 16-scene B4 diagnosis: 37/240 material errors selected a seed-positive lower-IoU query over a seed-negative oracle. Native unit and paired backward/resource tests pass; 4.75 and 6.396 GiB reserved on tested pairs, equal to B4.\n- H5 adds all-query attention at the last decoder layer. Fixed 16-scene diagnosis: 215/240 material-error selected/oracle pairs mutually outside final four nearest, though accessible in the first layer. Native distant-query and backward tests pass; 4.775/6.406 GiB reserved versus B4 4.750/6.396 GiB.\n- Both are testable, not proven gains or novelty. Admission receipts and evaluation freezes are in pipeline/admissions and pipeline/designs.\n\n## Closed Or Failed Directions\n- B0 0.333; B2-E30 0.5058; B3 0.5014; B4 20-epoch 0.5070; B5 0.5030; C1-E30 0.5008; C2-E30 0.5014; F4 0.5060; D1 0.5080. No repeat, scalar tuning or extension-only successor.\n- E1 stability, F1 entropy, F2 compactness and F3 seed proximity rejected by fixed B4 diagnoses.\n- H1 sampler omission: 0/240 material errors had available-but-dropped target seed. H2 four-per-query fine shortlist reduced coverage 0.70936 to 0.70842 on errors. H3 score-only selector 0.38265 versus B4 indicator 0.49186 subset mIoU. H4 relation cohort not enriched (204/387 errors versus 36/54 unmarked). All rejected; no validation scan.\n\n## Running And Queue\n- 2026-09-25 17:47 +08:00 prepared monitor: G1 server-2 GPU0, H5 server-2 GPU1, both 1/30 with no validation. Prior 17:33 native logs showed advancing steps (G1 PID 11694, H5 PID 36497); no fresh PID/GPU utilization reading this tick.\n- Active 2/2, no waiting or claiming. G1 commit 0f5f695d478b87750d69561428f6421833e629a9; H5 commit dafa28c03e6d13d68d2a572d9e725f4ed40227dc. Both nine-file additive syncs hash-verified; min_epochs=30 per task.\n\n## Open Questions And Risks\n- No pending questions in prepared manifest. Native probes are bounded; full-validation metrics, active queries, latency, peak memory, subgroup effects and evaluation noise are unknown.\n- Local Python lacks PyTorch; native tests ran on server-2. Remote code tree is not a Git checkout; scripts/sync.sh verified committed archive bytes. This project has no closure_policy.json. Receipt validation was local and dispatch used the locked queue dispatcher.\n- experiments.csv has malformed newer append rows; use experiment JSON and analyses. B4-E30 is a historical optimizer continuation, not a fresh matched control.\n\n## Last Tick\n- 2026-09-25 17:47 +08:00 event: completed preflight active 2/2; no new terminal IDs or due research work, candidate budget 0. No decision, queue change, admission or dispatch. Continue monitoring G1/H5 to terminal validation without tuning.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
